    "title": "March Madness 2026 NCAA tournament schedule tonight: Game time, TV channel, odds, picks, bracket",
    "text": "Updated March 18, 2026, 4:16 p.m. ETThe NCAA men's basketball tournament continues with First Four play-in games to finalize the 64-team bracket.Tonight's First Four games will be broadcast on truTV, with later games on CBS, TBS, and TNT.The First Round of the tournament begins on Thursday, March 19, with a full slate of games.The 2026 Final Four and championship game will take place at Lucas Oil Stadium in Indianapolis.The NCAA men's basketball tournament continues with First Four play-in round games tonight, narrowing the 2026 March Madness bracket field to 64 teams.Here's what to know on teams in the bracket, how to watch March Madness, NCAA tournament times, odds, picks and predictions:Where to watch 2026 March Madness bracket games tonight. What channel are 2026 NCAA tournament First Four play-in games on today?Today's NCAA men's basketball tournament games are on truTV. Along with truTV, March Madness games will be spread across CBS, TBS, TNT, and Paramount+ during the tournament.March Madness 2026 NCAA tournament bracket schedule of games tonight: Start time, TV channel, where to watch, stream every men's basketball game2026 NCAA tournament First Four March Madness games todnight: Wednesday, March 18(16) Prairie View A&M vs. (16) Lehigh, 6:40 p.m. ET, truTV | Preview / Box score(11) Miami (Ohio) vs. (11) SMU, 9:15 p.m. ET, truTV | Preview / Box scoreWatch NCAA men's basketball tournament action on Sling TV2026 NCAA tournament first round March Madness games: Thursday, March 19(8) Ohio State vs. (9) TCU, 12:15 p.m. ET, CBS | Preview(4) Nebraska vs. (13) Troy, 12:40 p.m. ET, truTV | Preview(6) Louisville vs. (11) South Florida, 1:30 p.m. ET, TNT | Preview(5) Wisconsin vs. (12) High Point, 1:50 p.m. ET, TBS | Preview(1) Duke vs. (16) Siena, 2:50 p.m. ET, CBS | Preview(5) Vanderbilt vs. (12) McNeese State, 3:15 p.m. ET, truTV | Preview(3) Michigan State vs. (14) North Dakota State, 4:05 p.m. ET, TNT | Preview(4) Arkansas vs. (13) Hawaii, 4:25 p.m. ET